Z||000006||William||02-22-2000||08:19 AM||||Would have to agree,The fast back looks great and I want one next, BUT, it looks like a very diffrent car then that first 84 Fiero that everyone fell in love with. AS a side note, If you look at a 84 -85 coupe and envision it with a fastback, it would seem that it would look alot like a Ferarri 308. However, if you compare a Fastback to a 308 it looks even less like one then the notchback, curious? I think the problem is that All fieros seem a little too tall. If roof was chopped 3 inches and the windsheild was raked more, I think that the fiero would have been more exotic looking. I would like to see a chop top fastback with a 84 nose just to see if it was a little closer to that 308. Can you tell I like thoses 308's?||||reg||14
